        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: canonicalize binary operation results",
        "body": "Closes #106047\n\nAI-assisted with Codex. Maintainer-requested refactor; transcript intentionally omitted at maintainer request.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nInternal binary operations used multiple weak `{ ok: boolean }` shapes, so TypeScript could not reliably narrow success payloads from errors. The repository already had a sound discriminated `Result`, but it was buried inside the agent-core harness and unavailable to core callers; agent-core also duplicated unknown-error coercion.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis promotes the tiny `Result<TValue, TError>` type plus `ok()` and `err()` to `@openclaw/normalization-core/result`, keeps the shipped agent-core exports compatible, and routes agent-core error coercion through normalization-core. Fitting internal operations now use discriminated results; public plugin SDK contracts, memory-host SDK contracts, and domain-rich outcomes remain unchanged. Package dist entries now derive from package exports so new subpaths cannot silently miss the build.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo CLI, config, or end-user behavior changes. Maintainers get compile-time narrowing for binary failures, structured error metadata survives agent-core coercion, and new fallible-operation results have one documented owner.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `578e0aecea65e6e9fbd168f186bc08c5bab060dd`.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcwmyzqkhy5atp4fzcye77y` ([run 29224666598](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29224666598)): `pnpm build`; 556 focused tests passed with 24 macOS-only skips; Plugin SDK API baseline passed; expected normalization-core `result`/`expect` dist artifacts present.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcx20hsyr4kqfwzrfb2qxjn` ([run 29224926865](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29224926865)): `pnpm tsgo:all` and `pnpm lint:scripts` passed.\n- Targeted `oxfmt --check` and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: no actionable findings; patch correct at 0.88 confidence.\n- `pnpm check:changed` reaches the repository-wide TypeScript LOC ratchet, which is already red on the exact base SHA for unrelated growth. Every touched over-baseline file shrinks relative to its baseline; the same base failure was reproduced before running the successful scoped/full gates above.\n\n### Deliberate exclusions\n\n- No combinator library; no current `map`/`andThen`/`unwrap` demand.\n- No mass rename of domain result payloads.\n- No change to `ChannelSendRawResult`, memory-host SDK result contracts, status flags, callbacks, or multi-arm outcomes.\n",
